          "filename": "StateLibQld 1 171479 Brisbane River, between New Farm and Hawthorne, during the 1931 flood.jpg",
          "caption": "Brisbane River, between New Farm and Hawthorne, during the 1931 flood.\nPeople gathered at the water's edge at Hawthorne with a view across to CSR refinery at New Farm, during the 1931 Brisbane floods. People have come on foot carrying umbrellas, or on bicycles to view the damage caused by the floodwaters. A number of children have waded out into the water. It was probably at the site of the Blondells Engineering on Scott Street. Today, the Hawthorn location is next to the Hawthorn Ferry terminal and Hardcastle Park. (Description supplied with photograph).",
